# CR-V Diag recording #3 — first full use of 0.11.0 on the car (excerpts)
# Date: 2026-11-18 · Tablet: Galaxy Tab A9+ · Adapter: V03H4 clone over Wi-Fi 192.168.0.10:35000
# Source: Advanced → Copy log, emailed by the owner as PDF; excerpts transcribed line by line (exact).
# Car state: engine running (warm idle, ATRV 13.6–14.1 V) except the clear-codes part (engine off, RPM 0).
# FINDINGS:
#  1. Late replies: the clone answers NO DATA early, then prints the real answer after its prompt, where the
#     app took it as the answer to the NEXT request (010D got the 410C answer, ...). Fixed in 0.12.0:
#     replies must match the request (service + PID), stale ones are skipped, late answers get 300 ms grace.
#  2. Junk after the prompt: tails of earlier, longer replies (">4\r18DAF11122...", ">C\r\r>") are repeated
#     by the clone's Wi-Fi bridge. Not from the app's reader (StreamTransport emits exactly n bytes).
#  3. Clear codes: both units answered 7F 04 78 (NRC 0x78 = "received, answer pending"), NOT a refusal.
#     The clear had worked (0101 afterwards: MIL off, 0 codes, monitors reset). Fixed in 0.12.0.
#  4. VIN: only the first ISO-TP frame arrived (consecutive frames dropped) → VIN missing. Fixed: retried.
#  5. Codes: P0497 + P145C pending at 21:22, STORED with MIL ON at 21:55 (0101 A=0x82), permanent (0A).
#  6. Mode 06 misfire counters: cylinder 3 = 9 this cycle / 5 average (21:58), others 0–1.
